  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proteccin del venado bura endmico de Isla Cedros mediante la erradicacin de perro feral</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the conservation and restoration of the species and ecosystems of Cedros Island by eradicating feral dogs and changing peoples practice of introducing invasive species to this unique place. This project intends to protect the endemic mule deer by reducing the impacts of predation by feral dogs. Specific activities include: (1) overflying of the island to estimate population size and distribution of feral dogs and mule deer; (2) eradication of feral dogs and sterilization of domestic dogs owned by the local communities; (3) planning and implementation of an outreach and awareness campaign for the local community; (4) a participative workshop for the local community members to develop a joint strategy to prevent the introduction of exotic species (biosecurity) to the island, particularly of domestic dogs and cats; and (5) development of a mule deer management plan.</narrative>
  </description>
